00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:05.434
For the primary keys, we can use
the Spring ID annotation here.

00:14:05.434 --> 00:14:07.100
But because Spanner
may actually require

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:10.750
you to use a composite key for
a parent-children relationships,

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:12.580
because we want you
to use composite keys

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.610
with multiple primary keys that
has interleaving in between,

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:17.920
so we actually have an
additional annotation here

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.586
